    "provinceDeepAtlasProfile": {
      "oneLine": "Falthrakar is centered at 32.804753, -5.451203 under Diarchy, with 118,613,000 people across 11 settlements.",
      "extremeAtlasDescription": "Falthrakar occupies 6,829,353.14 sq mi / 17,687,943.45 sq km of modeled Earth-sized territory, about 3.467776% of Belavadös's surface. It is not merely a province but a continent-scale civic machine: Partial forest, Beach and grass with water and Marshes and swamps define its broad terrain, while its settlements intensify into Beach and grass with water, Partial forest, Grassland, Marshes and swamps and Farming. Population density is 6.706 people/sq km / 17.368 people/sq mi, which lets wilderness, roads, faction-held corridors, and vast uncrowded borders remain huge.",
      "peopleFactionsAndFaith": "The strongest public people-groups are Humans, Near-Humans, and Mixed Heritage, Halfling and Smallfolk, Elf Parent Race and Elf Bloodlines, Animalfolk and Mammalian Anthropomorphs, Fey and Trickster Folk, Amphibious and Aquatic Peoples, and 2 more. Frequently recorded peoples include Human, Halfling — Lightfoot Halfling, Elf — Wood Elf, Elf — Eladrin, Fey-Folk — Faerie, Satyr, Changeling, Harengon, and 4 more. Faction visibility leans toward The Crucible Wardens, with worship and patronage records naming Nebyrr, Ishtanora, Marduthor, Setrimir, Sigrananna, Iskareth, Thalunesh, and 3 more.",
